2. REQUIRED ARCHITECTURE
==================================================

Implement this workflow:

User Message
    ↓
Authentication Context Resolver
    ↓
Conversation Context Resolver
    ↓
Intent and Domain Router
    ↓
Dynamic Business SOP Registry
    ↓
Business Semantic Contract Loader
    ↓
MongoDB Metadata Resolver
    ↓
Structured Query Planner
    ↓
Policy and Permission Validator
    ↓
MQL Generator
    ↓
MongoDB Query Checker
    ↓
Performance Preflight
    ↓
Read-Only Query Executor
    ↓
Result Validator and Normalizer
    ↓
Business Response Composer
    ↓
Audit and Conversation Memory

Use LangGraph for orchestration.

Create explicit LangGraph nodes for:

- resolve_context
- classify_intent
- load_business_contract
- resolve_schema
- create_query_plan
- validate_query_plan
- generate_mql
- check_mql
- performance_preflight
- execute_query
- validate_result
- compose_response
- save_audit
- request_clarification
- handle_error

Use conditional routing for:

- missing business context
- unsupported intent
- permission denied
- unsafe query
- invalid query
- expensive query
- empty result
- successful result

Do not use an unconstrained ReAct loop for the entire process.

Use a deterministic LangGraph workflow for query generation and execution.
A bounded agent step may be used only for collection/schema discovery when
the relevant collection cannot be determined deterministically.

Maximum agent iterations must be configurable and default to 4.

